# Observability

Observability means understanding what is happening inside the app.

In a RAG app, many things can go wrong:

```text
PDF loading fails
Embedding fails
Retriever finds wrong chunks
LLM gives weak answer
Token cost becomes high
Response is slow
```

Observability helps us see and fix those problems.

## What To Track

Track requests:

```text
Which endpoint was called?
How long did it take?
Did it fail?
```

Track indexing:

```text
Which file was indexed?
How many chunks were created?
How long did indexing take?
Did embedding fail?
```

Track retrieval:

```text
Which chunks were returned?
Which sources were used?
What was the top score?
```

Track LLM usage:

```text
prompt tokens
completion tokens
total tokens
model name
latency
errors
```

Track user experience:

```text
slow answers
failed uploads
empty answers
common questions
```

Track product activity:

```text
team created
team invite created
team invite accepted
team invite canceled
team member removed
document indexed
document renamed
document shared
document re-indexed
document deleted
```

## Simple Log Example

```js
{
  event: "chat_completed",
  question: "What is the salary of CX-MA-001?",
