  completionTokens: 262,
  durationMs: 4500
}
```

## Why It Matters

Without observability, we guess.

With observability, we can answer:

```text
Why was the answer wrong?
Was retrieval bad?
Was the LLM slow?
Did token usage increase?
Which document caused an error?
Who changed document sharing?
Who canceled an invite?
Which version was re-indexed?
```

## Current Implementation

The project now has an `activity_logs` table.

It stores:

```text
actor
action
entity type
entity ID
message
metadata
created date
```

The frontend shows:

```text
document activity timeline
team activity timeline
document version history
```

## Simple Presentation Version

```text
Observability means tracking logs, errors, token usage, retrieval sources, indexing status, document versions, and team/document activity so we can understand and improve the RAG app.
```
